        "at": "2026-10-09T14:22:51"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "SCARCE LABELS",
      "narration_text": "It matters most when labels are scarce. Cut the fine-tuning data to five spectra per class, and starting from the pretrained model is about four points ahead of scratch. With all ninety per class the gap narrows. Full fine-tuning stays one to two points ahead, and adapters drift back toward scratch.",
